cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use robo-cortex in your work, please cite the paper below."
title: "robo-cortex"
abstract: >-
  A local-first memory store for AI coding agents, built on the premise that
  machine memory is only as trustworthy as the code it points at. Memories are
  anchored to git blob hashes, so when the linked code changes they are
  automatically flagged for review instead of being silently trusted or lost;
  confidence is evidence-based. No embeddings, no vector database, no cloud —
  standard-library Python over SQLite, exposed via a CLI, a Python SDK, and
  eight Model Context Protocol (MCP) tools.
